# SynapseIDS API tokens — THUGS(red) SynapseIDS  (issue #58)
#
# Referenced by auth.tokens_file when auth.enabled is true. One line per token:
#
#     <role>   <token>   [free-text label...]
#
# role   : viewer | operator | admin  (cumulative — operator covers viewer, etc.)
# token  : >= 8 characters, opaque. Generate one with, e.g.:
#              head -c 24 /dev/urandom | base64
# label  : optional, ignored by the daemon, useful to you.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored. Keep this file 0600 and
# owned by the daemon user:
#
#     install -m 0600 -o synapse -g synapse tokens /etc/synapseids/tokens
#
# Clients send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the WebSocket route also takes
# `?token=<token>`. See docs/api.md#authentication-issue-58.

viewer    CHANGE-ME-read-only-wallboard      noc-wallboard
operator  CHANGE-ME-run-captures-replays     soc-analyst
admin     CHANGE-ME-full-control             ops-oncall
